## Terminology-robustness additions

The repository includes the four records added after the final terminology-robustness search:

1. State Contamination in Memory-Augmented LLM Agents;
2. ADAM: A Systematic Data Extraction Attack on Agent Memory via Adaptive Querying;
3. Defense Effectiveness Across Architectural Layers;
4. Towards Security-Auditable LLM Agents (Agent-BOM).

The master candidate map uses IDs 83–86, while the manuscript Appendix uses core IDs 68–71. The four mappings are recorded in `data/processed/id_crosswalk.csv` and explained in `docs/ID_CROSSWALK.md`.

## Scope of validation

The script checks record counts, unique identifiers, role totals, publication-status totals, all Yes/Partial/No capability values, role-disaggregated explicit support, non-benchmark values, peer-reviewed-only values, Appendix A coverage, and the four-row identifier crosswalk. It writes the machine-readable output to `analysis/derived_summary.json` and exits with a non-zero code when a required value does not match.

This report does not claim independent second-coder agreement, authenticated database-native hit counts where those exports are unavailable, or redistribution of copyrighted full texts.
